@export Is there a circumstance the Regulations name that could lead the Minister to waive the spouse or partner condition (Regs s 2(5))?
GIVEN `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is not resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner not resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act?
      `I am not living with them for reasons not attributable to me or to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not living with them for reasons that are not attributable to you or to them?
      `they have engaged in family violence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner engaged in family violence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a circumstance named in the Regulations for a waiver` IF
    `a circumstance named in subsection 2(5) is present` `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is not resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` `I am not living with them for reasons not attributable to me or to them` `they have engaged in family violence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act`

@export May the Minister waive the spouse or partner condition for me (Regs s 2(5))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that the condition is unreasonable or impracticable in my circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the condition is unreasonable or impracticable in your circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister waive the spouse or partner condition for me` IF
    `the Minister may waive the condition in subsection 2(4)` `the Minister is satisfied that the condition is unreasonable or impracticable in my circumstances`

@export Is my allocation suspended for this month because I asked for a suspension (Regs s 2(6), 11)?
GIVEN `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
