            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS FALSE
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`

-- Regs s 2.1 with SOR/2026-123 s 14. One payment is asked about; a person with several asks once for each (a single qualifying payment is enough).
@export Am I owed the supplemental amount (Regs s 2.1)?
GIVEN `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act?
      `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a payment of the benefit made to you after you obtained that certificate?
      `that payment is an allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment an allocation?
      `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that payment made before section 14 of SOR/2026-123 came into force?
      `I was entitled to that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to that payment?
      `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of that payment, was your status as a DTC-eligible individual based on that certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed the supplemental amount` IF
    `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` `my payments`
    WHERE
        `my payments` MEANS IF `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` THEN LIST (`Payment made after a certificate` WITH `the payment is an allocation` IS `that payment is an allocation`, `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force`, `the person was entitled to the payment` IS `I was entitled to that payment`, `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate`) ELSE EMPTY

@export How much is the supplemental amount (Regs s 6.1)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the supplemental amount` IS
    `the supplemental amount`

@export How is the supplemental amount paid (Regs s 9.1)?
GIVETH A `Form of payment`
DECIDE `How is the supplemental amount paid` IS
    `the form in which the supplemental amount is paid`

-- Act s 4: eligible if the person meets the criteria the Regulations set, for an allocation (s 2) or for the supplemental amount (s 2.1).
@export Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit (Act s 4)?
GIVEN `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a DTC-eligible individual (eligible for the disability tax credit) throughout that month?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout that month?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a temporary resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months immediately before that month have you been resident in Canada? (0 if you are not a temporary resident)
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a protected person under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act?
      `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving, or have you served, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more? (No if you have none)
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `I have been in custody under that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in custody under that sentence?
      `the first day I was in custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first go into custody under that sentence? (Any date if you were never in custody)
      `I have been released from that custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released from that custody?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you were not released)
      `the way I was released` IS A `Way of release` @desc How were you released: on earned remission, at the expiry of the sentence, on parole, or on statutory release?
      `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your parole or statutory release terminated or revoked? (No if you were not on one)
      `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began?
      `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner file a return of income for that year? (No if you have none)
      `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition that your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner must have filed a return of income?
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
      `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the suspension take effect? (Any date if you did not ask for one)
      `payment has resumed after my suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allocation resumed after the suspension?
      `a day in the month payment resumed` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the month payment resumed. (Any date if it has not resumed)
      `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act?
      `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a payment of the benefit made to you after you obtained that certificate?
      `that payment is an allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment an allocation?
      `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that payment made before section 14 of SOR/2026-123 came into force?
      `I was entitled to that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to that payment?
      `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of that payment, was your status as a DTC-eligible individual based on that certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for a Canada disability benefit` IF
    `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` `my facts` `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` `my payments`
    WHERE
        `my release` MEANS IF `I have been released from that custody` THEN JUST (`Release event` WITH `the day of the release` IS `the day I was released`, `the way of the release` IS `the way I was released`, `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my custody` MEANS IF `I have been in custody under that sentence` THEN JUST (`Custody under a sentence` WITH `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`, `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`, `the first day in custody` IS `the first day I was in custody`, `the release that ended the custody` IS `my release`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my suspension` MEANS IF `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` THEN JUST (`Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH `the day the suspension took effect` IS `the day my suspension took effect`, `a day in the month payment resumed` IS (IF `payment has resumed after my suspension` THEN JUST `a day in the month payment resumed` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING
        `my facts` MEANS `Person facts for a month` WITH
            `the month asked about` IS `the day of the month I am asking about`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`
            `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month`
            `a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen`
            `a permanent resident` IS `I am a permanent resident`
            `a temporary resident` IS `I am a temporary resident`
            `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month`
            `a protected person` IS `I am a protected person`
            `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`
            `the custody under a sentence` IS `my custody`
            `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began`
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year`
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`
        `my payments` MEANS IF `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` THEN LIST (`Payment made after a certificate` WITH `the payment is an allocation` IS `that payment is an allocation`, `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force`, `the person was entitled to the payment` IS `I was entitled to that payment`, `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate`) ELSE EMPTY


§§ `Regulations ss 4, 5 and 7 -- Applying, approval, and when the allocation begins`

@export On what day is my application treated as made (Regs s 4(2), 4(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your application?
      `the day the Minister received my application` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister receive your application? (Any date if not received)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my application treated as made` IS
    `the day an application is deemed to have been made` `my received day` `my date of birth`
    WHERE
        `my received day` MEANS IF `the Minister has received my application` THEN JUST `the day the Minister received my application` ELSE NOTHING

@export Do I have to make a new application (Regs s 4(4))?
GIVEN `payment of a benefit has been approved to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of a benefit been approved to you?
      `a benefit has become payable on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a benefit become payable on your behalf?
      `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a DTC-eligible individual (eligible for the disability tax credit) throughout that month?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout that month?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a temporary resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months immediately before that month have you been resident in Canada? (0 if you are not a temporary resident)
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a protected person under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act?
      `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving, or have you served, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more? (No if you have none)
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `I have been in custody under that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in custody under that sentence?
      `the first day I was in custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first go into custody under that sentence? (Any date if you were never in custody)
      `I have been released from that custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released from that custody?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you were not released)
      `the way I was released` IS A `Way of release` @desc How were you released: on earned remission, at the expiry of the sentence, on parole, or on statutory release?
      `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your parole or statutory release terminated or revoked? (No if you were not on one)
      `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began?
      `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner file a return of income for that year? (No if you have none)
      `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition that your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner must have filed a return of income?
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
      `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the suspension take effect? (Any date if you did not ask for one)
      `payment has resumed after my suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allocation resumed after the suspension?
      `a day in the month payment resumed` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the month payment resumed. (Any date if it has not resumed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have to make a new application` IF
    `the allocation has ceased and a new application is needed` `I am a beneficiary` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `I am a beneficiary` MEANS `the person is a beneficiary` `payment of a benefit has been approved to me` `a benefit has become payable on my behalf`
        `my release` MEANS IF `I have been released from that custody` THEN JUST (`Release event` WITH `the day of the release` IS `the day I was released`, `the way of the release` IS `the way I was released`, `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my custody` MEANS IF `I have been in custody under that sentence` THEN JUST (`Custody under a sentence` WITH `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`, `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`, `the first day in custody` IS `the first day I was in custody`, `the release that ended the custody` IS `my release`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my suspension` MEANS IF `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` THEN JUST (`Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH `the day the suspension took effect` IS `the day my suspension took effect`, `a day in the month payment resumed` IS (IF `payment has resumed after my suspension` THEN JUST `a day in the month payment resumed` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING
        `my facts` MEANS `Person facts for a month` WITH
            `the month asked about` IS `the day of the month I am asking about`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`
            `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month`
            `a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen`
            `a permanent resident` IS `I am a permanent resident`
            `a temporary resident` IS `I am a temporary resident`
            `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month`
            `a protected person` IS `I am a protected person`
            `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`
            `the custody under a sentence` IS `my custody`
            `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began`
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year`
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`

@export From what day is my application treated as approved (Regs s 5)?
GIVEN `the day my application is treated as made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application treated as made?
      `there is a month in which I met the criteria and for which no benefit was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a month in which you met all the criteria of section 2 and for which no benefit has been paid?
      `a day in the earliest such month` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the earliest such month. (Any date if there is none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what day is my application treated as approved` IS
    `the day an application is deemed to have been approved` `the day my application is treated as made` `my earliest eligible day`
    WHERE
        `my earliest eligible day` MEANS IF `there is a month in which I met the criteria and for which no benefit was paid` THEN JUST (`the first day of the month of` `a day in the earliest such month`) ELSE NOTHING

@export Which is the first month I am entitled to an allocation (Regs s 7)?
GIVEN `the day my application is treated as approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application treated as approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which is the first month I am entitled to an allocation` IS
    `the first month for which a beneficiary is entitled to an allocation` `the day my application is treated as approved`


§§ `Regulations ss 6 to 9 -- How the benefit is worked out and paid`

@export Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income (Regs s 6(1), 6(4.1))?
GIVEN `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner also a beneficiary of the Canada disability benefit?
      `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition about your spouse or partner filing a return of income?
GIVETH A `Subsection that works out the reduction`
DECIDE `Which part of section 6 works out my reduction for income` IS
    `which subsection works out the reduction` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Income and household facts` WITH
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary`
            `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS 0
            `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS 0
            `the beneficiary's own working income` IS `no working income`
            `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS `no working income`
        `no working income` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS 0
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0

-- Regs s 6. The Consumer Price Index is asked for 2024, 2025 and 2026, so a month from July 2028 on (the payment period that begins on
-- 1 July 2028 needs the 2027 index) comes back as not covered (NOTHING). So does a month in the payment period that
-- began on 1 July 2024 (June 2025), for which the Regulations give no indexing factor.
@export What is my basic amount for this month, worked out under section 6 (Regs s 6(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner also a beneficiary of the Canada disability benefit?
      `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition about your spouse or partner filing a return of income?
      `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your adjusted income (Income Tax Act s 122.6) for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began, not counting the income of anyone who was your spouse or partner at the end of that year?
      `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a spouse or partner now: what would your adjusted income for that year have been if they had been your spouse or partner at the end of it? (0 if you have none)
      `my working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your working income for that year? (the amounts in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act, plus your net farming, fishing, professional, commission and other business income)
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income for that year? (0 if you have none)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada for 2024 (annual average, not seasonally adjusted, as Statistics Canada publishes it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2025? (0 if it is not yet published)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2026? (0 if it is not yet published)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my basic amount for this month` IS
    `the basic amount payable for the month` `my payment period` `my figures` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my payment period` MEANS `the payment period that includes the day` `the day of the month I am asking about`
        `my figures` MEANS filter `has been published` (LIST `the 2024 figure`, `the 2025 figure`, `the 2026 figure`)
        `has been published` f MEANS f's `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` GREATER THAN 0
        `the 2024 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2024, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2024`
        `the 2025 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2025, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2025`
        `the 2026 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2026, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2026`
        `my household` MEANS `Income and household facts` WITH
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary`
            `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)`
            `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `the beneficiary's own working income` IS `my working income record`
            `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS `my partner's working income record`
        `my working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0
        `my partner's working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the partner's working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0

-- The formula can go below zero when the reduction is large (fork F9); this question shows the value as the formula gives it.
@export What does the section 6 formula give for me this month, before any floor at zero (Regs s 6(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner also a beneficiary of the Canada disability benefit?
      `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition about your spouse or partner filing a return of income?
      `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your adjusted income (Income Tax Act s 122.6) for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began, not counting the income of anyone who was your spouse or partner at the end of that year?
      `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a spouse or partner now: what would your adjusted income for that year have been if they had been your spouse or partner at the end of it? (0 if you have none)
      `my working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your working income for that year? (the amounts in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act, plus your net farming, fishing, professional, commission and other business income)
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income for that year? (0 if you have none)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada for 2024 (annual average, not seasonally adjusted, as Statistics Canada publishes it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2025? (0 if it is not yet published)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2026? (0 if it is not yet published)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What does the section 6 formula give for me this month` IS
    `the basic amount worked out by the formula for the month` `my payment period` `my figures` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my payment period` MEANS `the payment period that includes the day` `the day of the month I am asking about`
        `my figures` MEANS filter `has been published` (LIST `the 2024 figure`, `the 2025 figure`, `the 2026 figure`)
        `has been published` f MEANS f's `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` GREATER THAN 0
        `the 2024 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2024, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2024`
        `the 2025 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2025, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2025`
        `the 2026 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2026, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2026`
        `my household` MEANS `Income and household facts` WITH
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS `I have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month I am asking about`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary`
            `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)`
            `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `the beneficiary's own working income` IS `my working income record`
            `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS `my partner's working income record`
        `my working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0
        `my partner's working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the partner's working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0

-- Regs s 8(1) with s 7: entitled for a month that is not before the first month of s 7 and in which the criteria of section 2 are met.
@export Am I entitled to an allocation for this month (Regs s 8(1))?
GIVEN `a day in the first month I am entitled to an allocation` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the first month you are entitled to an allocation (the month after your application is treated as approved).
      `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a DTC-eligible individual (eligible for the disability tax credit) throughout that month?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout that month?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a temporary resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months immediately before that month have you been resident in Canada? (0 if you are not a temporary resident)
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a protected person under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act?
      `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving, or have you served, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more? (No if you have none)
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `I have been in custody under that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in custody under that sentence?
      `the first day I was in custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first go into custody under that sentence? (Any date if you were never in custody)
      `I have been released from that custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released from that custody?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you were not released)
      `the way I was released` IS A `Way of release` @desc How were you released: on earned remission, at the expiry of the sentence, on parole, or on statutory release?
      `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your parole or statutory release terminated or revoked? (No if you were not on one)
      `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began?
      `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner file a return of income for that year? (No if you have none)
      `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition that your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner must have filed a return of income?
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
      `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the suspension take effect? (Any date if you did not ask for one)
      `payment has resumed after my suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allocation resumed after the suspension?
      `a day in the month payment resumed` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the month payment resumed. (Any date if it has not resumed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to an allocation for this month` IF
    `the beneficiary is entitled to an allocation for the month` `a day in the first month I am entitled to an allocation` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my release` MEANS IF `I have been released from that custody` THEN JUST (`Release event` WITH `the day of the release` IS `the day I was released`, `the way of the release` IS `the way I was released`, `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my custody` MEANS IF `I have been in custody under that sentence` THEN JUST (`Custody under a sentence` WITH `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`, `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`, `the first day in custody` IS `the first day I was in custody`, `the release that ended the custody` IS `my release`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my suspension` MEANS IF `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` THEN JUST (`Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH `the day the suspension took effect` IS `the day my suspension took effect`, `a day in the month payment resumed` IS (IF `payment has resumed after my suspension` THEN JUST `a day in the month payment resumed` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING
        `my facts` MEANS `Person facts for a month` WITH
            `the month asked about` IS `the day of the month I am asking about`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`
            `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month`
            `a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen`
            `a permanent resident` IS `I am a permanent resident`
            `a temporary resident` IS `I am a temporary resident`
            `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month`
            `a protected person` IS `I am a protected person`
            `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`
            `the custody under a sentence` IS `my custody`
            `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began`
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year`
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`

-- Regs s 8(1) with s 6: the basic amount for a month in which I am entitled, and nothing for a month in which I am not.
-- The facts about a spouse or partner come from the answers about the condition in section 2(4); whether they are also a beneficiary is asked once.
@export How much allocation is payable to me this month (Regs s 8(1))?
GIVEN `a day in the first month I am entitled to an allocation` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the first month you are entitled to an allocation (the month after your application is treated as approved).
      `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a DTC-eligible individual (eligible for the disability tax credit) throughout that month?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout that month?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a temporary resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months immediately before that month have you been resident in Canada? (0 if you are not a temporary resident)
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a protected person under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act?
      `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving, or have you served, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more? (No if you have none)
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `I have been in custody under that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in custody under that sentence?
      `the first day I was in custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first go into custody under that sentence? (Any date if you were never in custody)
      `I have been released from that custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released from that custody?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you were not released)
      `the way I was released` IS A `Way of release` @desc How were you released: on earned remission, at the expiry of the sentence, on parole, or on statutory release?
      `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your parole or statutory release terminated or revoked? (No if you were not on one)
      `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began?
      `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner file a return of income for that year? (No if you have none)
      `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition that your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner must have filed a return of income?
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
      `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the suspension take effect? (Any date if you did not ask for one)
      `payment has resumed after my suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allocation resumed after the suspension?
      `a day in the month payment resumed` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the month payment resumed. (Any date if it has not resumed)
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner also a beneficiary of the Canada disability benefit?
      `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your adjusted income (Income Tax Act s 122.6) for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began, not counting the income of anyone who was your spouse or partner at the end of that year?
      `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If you have a spouse or partner now: what would your adjusted income for that year have been if they had been your spouse or partner at the end of it? (0 if you have none)
      `my working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your working income for that year? (the amounts in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act, plus your net farming, fishing, professional, commission and other business income)
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income for that year? (0 if you have none)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada for 2024 (annual average, not seasonally adjusted, as Statistics Canada publishes it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2025? (0 if it is not yet published)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2026? (0 if it is not yet published)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much allocation is payable to me this month` IS
    `the allocation payable for the month` `a day in the first month I am entitled to an allocation` `my facts` `my household` `my figures`
    WHERE
        `my release` MEANS IF `I have been released from that custody` THEN JUST (`Release event` WITH `the day of the release` IS `the day I was released`, `the way of the release` IS `the way I was released`, `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my custody` MEANS IF `I have been in custody under that sentence` THEN JUST (`Custody under a sentence` WITH `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`, `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`, `the first day in custody` IS `the first day I was in custody`, `the release that ended the custody` IS `my release`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my suspension` MEANS IF `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` THEN JUST (`Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH `the day the suspension took effect` IS `the day my suspension took effect`, `a day in the month payment resumed` IS (IF `payment has resumed after my suspension` THEN JUST `a day in the month payment resumed` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING
        `my facts` MEANS `Person facts for a month` WITH
            `the month asked about` IS `the day of the month I am asking about`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`
            `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month`
            `a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen`
            `a permanent resident` IS `I am a permanent resident`
            `a temporary resident` IS `I am a temporary resident`
            `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month`
            `a protected person` IS `I am a protected person`
            `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`
            `the custody under a sentence` IS `my custody`
            `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began`
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year`
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`
        `my figures` MEANS filter `has been published` (LIST `the 2024 figure`, `the 2025 figure`, `the 2026 figure`)
        `has been published` f MEANS f's `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` GREATER THAN 0
        `the 2024 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2024, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2024`
        `the 2025 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2025, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2025`
        `the 2026 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2026, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2026`
        `my household` MEANS `Income and household facts` WITH
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month that precedes the month` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is also a beneficiary`
            `the Minister waived the condition in subsection 2(4)` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `adjusted income without the income of a person who was the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income without the income of a person who was my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `adjusted income as if the current spouse or partner had been the spouse or partner at the end of the year` IS `my adjusted income as if my current spouse or partner had been my spouse or partner at the end of the year`
            `the beneficiary's own working income` IS `my working income record`
            `the working income of the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner` IS `my partner's working income record`
        `my working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
            `net commission income` IS 0
            `other net business income` IS 0
        `my partner's working income record` MEANS `Working income` WITH
            -- All of the partner's working income is entered in the first field: the rule reads only the total of the six.
            `amounts referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition working income in subsection 122.7(1) of the Income Tax Act` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner's working income`
            `net farming income` IS 0
            `net fishing income` IS 0
            `net professional income` IS 0
