@export Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period (Regs s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the allocation payable to me in a month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much allocation is payable to you in a month, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my allocation be paid as one lump sum for the whole payment period` IF
    `the allocation is paid as a lump sum for the payment period` `the allocation payable to me in a month`

@export How big would my lump sum for the payment period be (Regs s 8(2))?
GIVEN `my basic amount for a month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic amount for a month, in dollars?
      `a day in the first month my allocation is payable in the payment period` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the first month your allocation is payable in the payment period.
      `a day in the payment period` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the payment period you are asking about.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How big would my lump sum for the payment period be` IS
    `the lump sum for the payment period` `my basic amount for a month` (`the first day of the month of` `a day in the first month my allocation is payable in the payment period`) (`the payment period that includes the day` `a day in the payment period`)

-- Regs s 9 sums the amounts worked out under section 6 for each month from the month after approval through the month of the first
-- payment. This question uses one amount for every month; a person whose amount changes across 1 July asks month by month.
@export What will my first payment of the allocation be (Regs s 9)?
GIVEN `the day my application is treated as approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your application treated as approved?
      `the day my first payment is made` IS A DATE @desc On what day is your first payment made?
      `my allocation for a month, the same each month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your allocation for a month, in dollars? (The same amount is used for every month from the month after approval to the month of the first payment.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What will my first payment of the allocation be` IS
    `the first payment of an allocation` `the day my application is treated as approved` `the day my first payment is made` (replicate `the number of months` `my allocation for a month, the same each month`)
    WHERE
        `the number of months` MEANS `the number of months from the month of` `the day my application is treated as approved` `to the month of` `the day my first payment is made`


§§ `Regulations ss 10 and 11 -- Suspension of payments`

@export Can the Minister suspend my payments (Regs s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that I do not meet the eligibility criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister have reasonable grounds to believe that you do not meet the eligibility criteria of section 2?
      `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry into my eligibility is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister have reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry into your eligibility is necessary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister suspend my payments` IF
    `the Minister may suspend payment of the allocation` `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that I do not meet the eligibility criteria` `the Minister has reasonable grounds to believe that an inquiry into my eligibility is necessary`

@export Can the Minister keep my payments suspended (Regs s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that I am eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister now satisfied that you are eligible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister keep my payments suspended` IF
    `the Minister may keep payment of the allocation suspended` `the Minister is satisfied that I am eligible`

@export Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility (Regs s 10(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister suspended my payments under subsection 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister suspended your payments because of doubts about your eligibility?
      `a reasonable time has passed since the suspension began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a reasonable time passed since the suspension began?
      `the Minister has reviewed my eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister reviewed your eligibility?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Minister taken too long to review my eligibility` IF
    `the Minister has not reviewed the beneficiary's eligibility within a reasonable time` `the Minister suspended my payments under subsection 10(1)` `a reasonable time has passed since the suspension began` `the Minister has reviewed my eligibility`

@export Must the Minister resume my payments and pay me what I missed (Regs s 10(3))?
GIVEN `the suspension has been lifted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the suspension been lifted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister resume my payments and pay me what I missed` IF
    `the Minister must resume payment and pay a lump sum` `the suspension has been lifted`

-- Regs s 10(3) sums the amounts worked out under section 6 for each month of the suspension. This question uses one amount for every month.
@export How much will I be paid when the Minister lifts a suspension (Regs s 10(3))?
GIVEN `my allocation for a month, the same each month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is your allocation for a month, in dollars?
      `the number of months the suspension lasted` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months did the suspension last?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be paid when the Minister lifts a suspension` IS
    `the lump sum on lifting a suspension` (replicate `the number of months the suspension lasted` `my allocation for a month, the same each month`)

@export On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them (Regs s 11(1), 11(2))?
GIVEN `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing?
      `the day the Minister processes my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the Minister process your request?
      `my request names a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request name a day for the suspension to start?
      `the day my request names` IS A DATE @desc What day does your request name? (Any date if it names none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day would my payments stop if I ask the Minister to suspend them` IS
    `the day on which payment of the allocation is suspended` `my request is in writing` `the day the Minister processes my request` `the day my request names, if any`
    WHERE
        `the day my request names, if any` MEANS IF `my request names a day` THEN JUST `the day my request names` ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my request to resume payments in time (Regs s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your suspension take effect?
      `the day the Minister received my request to resume` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister receive your request to resume?
      `my request to resume is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request to resume in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request to resume payments in time` IF
    `a request to resume payment is made in time` `the day my suspension took effect` `the day the Minister received my request to resume` `my request to resume is in writing`

@export Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time (Regs s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your suspension take effect?
      `the Minister received a request to resume in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister receive, within 24 months after the suspension, your written request to resume?
      `the day the Minister received it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister receive it? (Any date if none)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my allocation ended because I did not ask to resume in time` IF
    `the allocation is deemed to have ceased and a new application is needed` `the day my suspension took effect` `my request received in time` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my request received in time` MEANS IF `the Minister received a request to resume in time` THEN JUST `the day the Minister received it` ELSE NOTHING

@export Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask (Regs s 11(4))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my request to resume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your request to resume payments?
      `the Minister is satisfied that I meet the eligibility criteria of section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that you meet the eligibility criteria of section 2?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister resume my payments when I ask` IF
    `the Minister must resume payment of the allocation` `the Minister has received my request to resume` `the Minister is satisfied that I meet the eligibility criteria of section 2`

@export In which month will my payments resume (Regs s 11(5))?
GIVEN `the day the Minister received my request to resume` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister receive your request to resume?
      `my request names a month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request name a month for payments to resume?
      `a day in the month my request names` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in that month. (Any date if it names none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month will my payments resume` IS
    `the month in which payment of the allocation resumes` `the day the Minister received my request to resume` `the month my request names, if any`
    WHERE
        `the month my request names, if any` MEANS IF `my request names a month` THEN JUST `a day in the month my request names` ELSE NOTHING


§§ `Regulations ss 12 to 16 -- Death of a beneficiary, and representatives`

@export Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died (Regs s 12)?
GIVEN `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beneficiary died?
      `my relationship to the beneficiary` IS A `Relationship to a deceased beneficiary` @desc What is your relationship to the beneficiary: executor or administrator of the estate, liquidator of the succession, heir, or none of these?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Minister that a beneficiary has died` IF
    `the person must notify the Minister of the beneficiary's death` `the beneficiary has died` `my relationship to the beneficiary`

@export Can the estate or the heirs claim the allocation for the month the beneficiary died (Regs s 13(1))?
GIVEN `the beneficiary has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beneficiary died?
      `the beneficiary received the allocation payment for the month in which they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the beneficiary receive the allocation payment for the month in which they died?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the estate or the heirs claim the allocation for the month of death` IF
    `the estate or succession or the heirs are eligible to receive the allocation payment for the month of death` `the beneficiary has died` `the beneficiary received the allocation payment for the month in which they died`

@export Who is paid an amount owing when a beneficiary dies (Regs s 13(2))?
GIVEN `the beneficiary has heirs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the beneficiary have heirs?
GIVETH A `Recipient of an amount owing on a death`
DECIDE `Who is paid an amount owing when a beneficiary dies` IS
    `who receives an amount owing on the death of a beneficiary` `the beneficiary has heirs`

@export Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared (Regs s 14(1))?
GIVEN `I have disappeared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you disappeared?
      `the Minister concludes that the circumstances raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that I am dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister conclude that the circumstances of the disappearance raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that you are dead?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister fix a date on which my death is presumed if I have disappeared` IF
    `the Minister may determine the date on which the beneficiary's death is presumed to have occurred` `I have disappeared` `the Minister concludes that the circumstances raise, beyond a reasonable doubt, a presumption that I am dead`

@export Will I be paid if the Minister changes the date of a presumed death or finds the beneficiary alive (Regs s 14(2), 14(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister has fixed a different date of death on new information or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister fixed a different date of death on the basis of new information or evidence?
      `the Minister is satisfied on new information or evidence that I am alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied, on new information or evidence, that you are alive?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the benefit be paid if the Minister changes the presumed date of death or finds me alive` IF
    `the Minister must pay any benefit that would have been payable had the first determination not been made` `the Minister has fixed a different date of death on new information or evidence` `the Minister is satisfied on new information or evidence that I am alive`

@export May my representative act for me (Regs s 15)?
GIVEN `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of managing your own affairs?
      `the other person is my representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who wants to act for you your representative?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my representative act for me` IF
    `the representative may act on the person's behalf` `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` `the other person is my representative`

@export May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative (Regs s 16)?
GIVEN `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of managing your own affairs?
      `my representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage my affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your representative authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage your affairs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister pay my benefit to my representative` IF
    `the Minister may direct that the benefit be paid on the beneficiary's behalf to their representative` `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` `my representative is authorized by or under a law of Canada or of a province to manage my affairs`


§§ `Regulations ss 17 to 19 and 31 -- Challenging a decision, and more time`

@export Can the Minister change a decision made about me (Regs s 17)?
GIVEN `the Minister made the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister make the decision?
      `new facts have come to the Minister's attention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have new facts come to the Minister's attention?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister change a decision made about me` IF
    `the Minister may amend or rescind the decision` `the Minister made the decision` `new facts have come to the Minister's attention`

@export Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision (Regs s 18(1), 18(2))?
GIVEN `the decision I disagree with` IS A `Decision of the Minister` @desc What kind of decision are you asking about: no benefit paid, the amount of a benefit, a penalty, a decision on a request for reconsideration, a decision on a request for an extension, or any other decision?
      `I am dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask the Minister to reconsider this decision` IF
    `the decision is one the person may ask the Minister to reconsider` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
            `the decision` IS `the decision I disagree with`
            `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS `I am dissatisfied with the decision`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

@export By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision (Regs s 18(1), 18(2))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I ask the Minister to reconsider a decision` IS
    `the last day of the 180 days to ask the Minister to reconsider` `the day I was notified in writing of the decision`

@export Is my request for reconsideration in time (Regs s 18, 19)?
GIVEN `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
      `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you (or will you) make your request for reconsideration?
      `the Minister extended the 180 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister extend the 180 days?
      `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days? (Any date if not extended)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my request for reconsideration in time` IF
    `the request was made in time` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
            `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS `the day I was notified in writing of the decision`
            `the day the request was made` IS `the day I made my request`
            `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS (IF `the Minister extended the 180 days` THEN JUST `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` ELSE NOTHING)
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS TRUE

@export Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require (Regs s 18(3))?
GIVEN `my request is in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing to the Minister?
      `my request gives my name and address and my Social Insurance Number or the application reference number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your name and address and your Social Insurance Number or the reference number of your application?
      `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of managing your own affairs?
      `my request gives the name and address of my representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give the name and address of your representative? (Only needed if you are incapable of managing your own affairs)
      `my request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request identify the decision and state the reasons and facts for the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my request for reconsideration say what the Regulations require` IF
    `the request has the contents the Regulations require` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the decision` IS `a decision that no benefit be paid to the person`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS YMD 2026 1 1
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the day the request was made` IS YMD 2026 6 30
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS NOTHING
            `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS `my request is in writing to the Minister`
            `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS `my request gives my name and address and my Social Insurance Number or the application reference number`
            `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS `I am incapable of managing my own affairs`
            `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS `my request gives the name and address of my representative`
            `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS `my request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request`

@export Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons (Regs s 18(4))?
GIVEN `the decision I disagree with` IS A `Decision of the Minister` @desc What kind of decision are you asking about: no benefit paid, the amount of a benefit, a penalty, a decision on a request for reconsideration, a decision on a request for an extension, or any other decision?
      `I am dissatisfied with the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with the decision?
      `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
      `the day I made my request` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you (or will you) make your request for reconsideration?
      `the Minister extended the 180 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister extend the 180 days?
      `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days? (Any date if not extended)
      `my request is in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing to the Minister?
      `my request gives my name and address and my Social Insurance Number or the application reference number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give your name and address and your Social Insurance Number or the reference number of your application?
      `I am incapable of managing my own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you incapable of managing your own affairs?
      `my request gives the name and address of my representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request give the name and address of your representative? (Only needed if you are incapable of managing your own affairs)
      `my request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your request identify the decision and state the reasons and facts for the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister reconsider my decision and give me written reasons` IF
    `the Minister must reconsider the decision and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reasons` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `Request for reconsideration` WITH
            `the decision` IS `the decision I disagree with`
            `the person is dissatisfied with the decision` IS `I am dissatisfied with the decision`
            `the day the person was notified in writing of the decision` IS `the day I was notified in writing of the decision`
            `the day the request was made` IS `the day I made my request`
            `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` IS (IF `the Minister extended the 180 days` THEN JUST `the last day to which the Minister extended the 180 days` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the request is made in writing to the Minister` IS `my request is in writing to the Minister`
            `the request gives the name and address of the applicant or the beneficiary and their Social Insurance Number or the reference number of the application` IS `my request gives my name and address and my Social Insurance Number or the application reference number`
            `the person is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS `I am incapable of managing my own affairs`
            `the request gives the name and address of their representative` IS `my request gives the name and address of my representative`
            `the request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request` IS `my request identifies the decision and states the reasons and facts for the request`

@export By what day must I ask the Minister for more time (Regs s 19(1))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I ask the Minister for more time` IS
    `the last day to ask the Minister to extend the 180 days` `the day I was notified in writing of the decision`

@export Must the Minister allow me more time (Regs s 19(3))?
GIVEN `the situation that kept me from acting in time` IS A `Situation affecting a time limit` @desc Which situation kept you from acting in time: an emergency, a disaster, a civil disturbance, a disruption in public services, a serious accident, injury or illness suffered by you, an emotional or mental distress suffered by you, or none of these?
      `the Minister is satisfied that it occurred and significantly impacted my ability to respect the time period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the situation occurred and significantly impacted your ability to respect the time period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister allow me more time` IF
    `the Minister must allow an extension of time` `the situation that kept me from acting in time` `the Minister is satisfied that it occurred and significantly impacted my ability to respect the time period`

@export Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason (Regs s 19(2), 19(4))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified in writing of the decision?
      `the day I made my request for an extension` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make your request for more time?
      `my request for an extension is in the form and manner the Minister specifies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your request for more time in the form and manner the Minister specifies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister consider my request for more time and tell me the reason` IF
    `the Minister must consider the request for an extension and notify the person in writing of the decision and the reason` `the day I was notified in writing of the decision` `the day I made my request for an extension` `my request for an extension is in the form and manner the Minister specifies`

@export Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit (Regs s 31)?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there was an administrative error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that there was an administrative error in the administration of the Act or the Regulations?
      `I was denied a benefit or a portion of a benefit as a result of the error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you denied a benefit, or part of one, as a result of the error?
      `I would have been entitled to what I was denied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you have been entitled to what you were denied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister put right an administrative error that cost me benefit` IF
    `the Minister must take remedial action to put the person in the position they would be in` `the Minister is satisfied that there was an administrative error` `I was denied a benefit or a portion of a benefit as a result of the error` `I would have been entitled to what I was denied`


§§ `Act s 10.1 and Regulations ss 20 to 29 -- Appeals`

@export Does the Act let me appeal this decision (Act s 10.1)?
GIVEN `the decision relates to my ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision relate to your ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit?
      `the decision relates to the amount of a Canada disability benefit I have received or will receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the decision relate to the amount of a Canada disability benefit you have received or will receive?
      `the decision is one the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision one that the Regulations prescribe for an appeal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act let me appeal this decision` IF
    `the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` `the decision relates to my ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit` `the decision relates to the amount of a Canada disability benefit I have received or will receive` `the decision is one the regulations prescribe`

@export How can I challenge this decision (Regs s 20)?
GIVEN `the decision I disagree with` IS A `Decision of the Minister` @desc What kind of decision are you asking about: no benefit paid, the amount of a benefit, a penalty, a decision on a request for reconsideration, a decision on a request for an extension, or any other decision?
GIVETH A `Way to challenge a decision`
DECIDE `How can I challenge this decision` IS
    `how the person may challenge the decision` `the decision I disagree with`

@export Who decides a ground of my appeal that says the Minister got my income wrong (Regs s 21, 29)?
GIVEN `the ground says a decision or determination of the Minister as to income was incorrectly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this ground of your appeal say that a decision or determination of the Minister as to income was incorrectly made?
GIVETH A `Body that decides a ground of appeal`
DECIDE `Who decides a ground of my appeal that says the Minister got my income wrong` IS
    `who decides the ground of appeal` `the ground says a decision or determination of the Minister as to income was incorrectly made`

@export Will the Tribunal now go on to the other grounds of my appeal (Regs s 29)?
GIVEN `my appeal sets out a ground sent to the Court and a ground not sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your appeal set out both a ground that was sent to the Tax Court and a ground that was not?
      `the Tribunal has received a certified copy of the Court's decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Social Security Tribunal received a certified copy of the Tax Court's decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Tribunal now go on to the other grounds of my appeal` IF
    `the Social Security Tribunal must now proceed on the grounds not referred, under its Rules of Procedure` `my appeal sets out a ground sent to the Court and a ground not sent` `the Tribunal has received a certified copy of the Court's decision`

@export Will another person be made a party to my appeal (Regs s 23)?
GIVEN `my appeal is about a decision or determination as to income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal about a decision or determination as to income?
      `the Minister is of the opinion that another person may be directly affected by the Court's decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister of the opinion that a person other than you may be directly affected by the decision of the Court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will another person be made a party to my appeal` IF
    `the other person is added as a party to the appeal` `my appeal is about a decision or determination as to income` `the Minister is of the opinion that another person may be directly affected by the Court's decision`

@export Where will the hearing of my reference be held (Regs s 24(2))?
GIVEN `I consent in writing to a different place or to a hearing by audioconference or videoconference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent in writing to the hearing being held, in whole or in part, at some other place or by audioconference or videoconference or both?
GIVETH A `Place of a hearing`
DECIDE `Where will the hearing of my reference be held` IS
    `where the hearing of a reference is held` `I consent in writing to a different place or to a hearing by audioconference or videoconference`

@export Must the Registrar tell me by registered mail when my hearing is set (Regs s 24(3))?
GIVEN `the date, place and time of my hearing have been set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the date, place and time of your hearing been set?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Registrar tell me by registered mail when my hearing is set` IF
    `the Registrar must notify the appellant by registered mail of the date, place and time` `the date, place and time of my hearing have been set`

@export Can the judge make me file written submissions (Regs s 26)?
GIVEN `I consent to written submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consent to filing written submissions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the judge make me file written submissions` IF
    `the judge may require written submissions` `I consent to written submissions`

@export Can I be made to pay costs or fees on a reference to the Tax Court (Regs s 28)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be made to pay costs or fees on a reference to the Tax Court` IF
    `costs may be awarded or fees charged to the appellant on a reference`


§§ `Act ss 5 to 7 and Regulations ss 32 to 34 -- Being paid, and what I must give or tell the Minister`

-- Act s 5 gathers three conditions: eligible (Act s 4), applied in accordance with the regulations, and any other condition the regulations set.
-- What is paid, and from which month, is Regs ss 6 to 9.
@export Must the Minister pay me a Canada disability benefit (Act s 5)?
GIVEN `the day of the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? Give any day in that month.
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a DTC-eligible individual (eligible for the disability tax credit) throughout that month?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout that month?
      `I am a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a Canadian citizen?
      `I am a permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a permanent resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am a temporary resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a temporary resident under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months immediately before that month have you been resident in Canada? (0 if you are not a temporary resident)
      `I am a protected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a protected person under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act?
      `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act?
      `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving, or have you served, a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more? (No if you have none)
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `I have been in custody under that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in custody under that sentence?
      `the first day I was in custody` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you first go into custody under that sentence? (Any date if you were never in custody)
      `I have been released from that custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been released from that custody?
      `the day I was released` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you released? (Any date if you were not released)
      `the way I was released` IS A `Way of release` @desc How were you released: on earned remission, at the expiry of the sentence, on parole, or on statutory release?
      `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your parole or statutory release terminated or revoked? (No if you were not on one)
      `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a return of income under the Income Tax Act for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began?
      `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before the month you are asking about?
      `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner file a return of income for that year? (No if you have none)
      `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the condition that your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner must have filed a return of income?
      `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the Minister, in writing, to suspend payment of your allocation?
      `the day my suspension took effect` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the suspension take effect? (Any date if you did not ask for one)
      `payment has resumed after my suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allocation resumed after the suspension?
      `a day in the month payment resumed` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the month payment resumed. (Any date if it has not resumed)
      `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act?
      `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a payment of the benefit made to you after you obtained that certificate?
      `that payment is an allocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that payment an allocation?
      `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that payment made before section 14 of SOR/2026-123 came into force?
      `I was entitled to that payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to that payment?
      `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of that payment, was your status as a DTC-eligible individual based on that certificate?
      `the person applies or an application is made on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the benefit, or has an application been made on your behalf, in accordance with the Regulations?
      `I meet any other condition the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet any other condition the Regulations set for receiving the benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister pay me a Canada disability benefit` IF
    `the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` (`the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` `my facts` `I obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` `my payments`) `the person applies or an application is made on my behalf` `I meet any other condition the regulations set`
    WHERE
        `my release` MEANS IF `I have been released from that custody` THEN JUST (`Release event` WITH `the day of the release` IS `the day I was released`, `the way of the release` IS `the way I was released`, `the parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked` IS `my parole or statutory release was terminated or revoked`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my custody` MEANS IF `I have been in custody under that sentence` THEN JUST (`Custody under a sentence` WITH `the sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more` IS `my sentence of imprisonment is of two years or more`, `the sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament`, `the first day in custody` IS `the first day I was in custody`, `the release that ended the custody` IS `my release`) ELSE NOTHING
        `my suspension` MEANS IF `I asked the Minister to suspend my allocation` THEN JUST (`Suspension at the beneficiary's request` WITH `the day the suspension took effect` IS `the day my suspension took effect`, `a day in the month payment resumed` IS (IF `payment has resumed after my suspension` THEN JUST `a day in the month payment resumed` ELSE NOTHING)) ELSE NOTHING
        `my facts` MEANS `Person facts for a month` WITH
            `the month asked about` IS `the day of the month I am asking about`
            `date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month` IS `I am a DTC-eligible individual throughout the month`
            `resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month` IS `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act throughout the month`
            `a Canadian citizen` IS `I am a Canadian citizen`
            `a permanent resident` IS `I am a permanent resident`
            `a temporary resident` IS `I am a temporary resident`
            `months resident in Canada immediately before the month` IS `the months I lived in Canada immediately before the month`
            `a protected person` IS `I am a protected person`
            `an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Indian Act`
            `the custody under a sentence` IS `my custody`
            `a return of income was filed for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began` IS `I filed a return of income for the last taxation year that ended before the payment period began`
            `a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before` IS `I had a cohabiting spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the month before`
            `the cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year` IS `my cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return of income for that year`
            `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition` IS `the Minister waived the spouse or partner condition`
            `the suspension the beneficiary asked for` IS `my suspension`
        `my payments` MEANS IF `an allocation or a benefit payment was made to me after I obtained the certificate` THEN LIST (`Payment made after a certificate` WITH `the payment is an allocation` IS `that payment is an allocation`, `the payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force` IS `that payment was made before SOR/2026-123 section 14 came into force`, `the person was entitled to the payment` IS `I was entitled to that payment`, `the status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of the payment rests on that certificate` IS `my status as a DTC-eligible individual at the time of that payment rests on that certificate`) ELSE EMPTY

@export Must I give the Minister the information they ask for about my application (Act s 6)?
GIVEN `I have applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a benefit?
      `an application for a benefit has been made on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for a benefit been made on your behalf?
      `I am the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs?
      `the Minister requires the information in respect of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require the information in respect of the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Minister the information they ask for about my application` IF
    `the person must provide the Minister with the information` `I am an applicant` `I am the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs` `the Minister requires the information in respect of the application`
    WHERE
        `I am an applicant` MEANS `the person is an applicant` `I have applied for a benefit` `an application for a benefit has been made on my behalf`

@export Can the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number (Act s 7)?
GIVEN `I have applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for a benefit?
      `an application for a benefit has been made on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for a benefit been made on your behalf?
      `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose the administration or enforcement of the Canada Disability Benefit Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister collect and use my Social Insurance Number` IF
    `the Minister is authorized to collect and use the person's Social Insurance Number` `I am an applicant` `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of the Act`
    WHERE
        `I am an applicant` MEANS `the person is an applicant` `I have applied for a benefit` `an application for a benefit has been made on my behalf`

@export Must I give the Minister the information or document in their notice (Regs s 32(2), 32(3))?
GIVEN `the kind of person I am` IS A `Kind of person asked for information` @desc Which are you: an applicant, a beneficiary, the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs, or any other person?
      `the notice was served on me personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice served on you personally or by confirmed delivery service?
      `the notice gives a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice give a reasonable time to provide the information or document?
      `a judge authorized the Minister and the authorization came with the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a judge authorize the Minister to require it, and was the authorization served with the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Minister the information or document in their notice` IF
    `the person is required to provide the information or document` `the kind of person I am` `the notice was served on me personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice gives a reasonable time` `a judge authorized the Minister and the authorization came with the notice`

@export By what day can I apply to a judge to review an authorization served on me (Regs s 32(6))?
GIVEN `the day the authorization and notice were served on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the authorization and the notice served on you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day can I apply to a judge to review an authorization served on me` IS
    `the last day to apply for a review of the authorization` `the day the authorization and notice were served on me`

@export Can the Minister require me to be at a place or available at a time (Regs s 34)?
GIVEN `the kind of person I am` IS A `Kind of person asked for information` @desc Which are you: an applicant, a beneficiary, the representative of an applicant or beneficiary who is incapable of managing their own affairs, or any other person?
      `the Minister requires it to verify compliance or to prevent non-compliance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister require it for a purpose related to verifying compliance or preventing non-compliance with the Act or the Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister require me to be at a place or available at a time` IF
    `the person is required to be at a suitable place or available at a suitable time` `the kind of person I am` `the Minister requires it to verify compliance or to prevent non-compliance`


§§ `Regulations ss 35 and 36 -- Penalties and offences`

@export Have I committed a violation (Regs s 35(1))?
GIVEN `I knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make a false or misleading representation in relation to an application for the benefit?
      `I made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing I was not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application for, and receive, the benefit knowing that you were not eligible to receive it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed a violation` IF
    `the person commits a violation` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Violation facts` WITH
            `knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application` IS `I knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application`
            `made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing they were not eligible to receive it` IS `I made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing I was not eligible`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the person mistakenly believed the representation true or believed they were eligible` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `a prosecution for the act has been initiated against the person` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the Minister became aware of the act on` IS YMD 2026 3 10

@export Can the Minister impose a penalty on me (Regs s 35(2), 35(5), 35(6))?
GIVEN `the Minister is of the opinion that I committed a violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister of the opinion, based on documents or information collected or obtained, that you committed a violation?
      `I knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make a false or misleading representation in relation to an application for the benefit?
      `I made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing I was not eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make an application for, and receive, the benefit knowing that you were not eligible to receive it?
      `I mistakenly believed the representation true or believed I was eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you mistakenly believe that a representation was true, or that you (or the person for whom you applied) were eligible?
      `a prosecution for the act has been started against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the act been started against you?
      `the day the Minister became aware of the act` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Minister become aware of the act?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister impose a penalty on me` IF
    `the Minister may impose a penalty` `the Minister is of the opinion that I committed a violation` `my facts` `the day I am asking about`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Violation facts` WITH
            `knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application` IS `I knowingly made a false or misleading representation in relation to an application`
            `made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing they were not eligible to receive it` IS `I made an application for, and received, a benefit knowing I was not eligible`
            `the person mistakenly believed the representation true or believed they were eligible` IS `I mistakenly believed the representation true or believed I was eligible`
            `a prosecution for the act has been initiated against the person` IS `a prosecution for the act has been started against me`
            `the Minister became aware of the act on` IS `the day the Minister became aware of the act`

@export Is this a first violation for me (Regs s 35(4))?
GIVEN `the day the violation occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the violation occur?
      `a penalty was imposed on me under section 35 before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a penalty imposed on you under section 35 on an earlier occasion? (Ask about the most recent one.)
      `the day that earlier penalty was imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was that earlier penalty imposed? (Any date if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a first violation for me` IF
    `the violation is deemed to be a first violation` `the day the violation occurred` `my penalty days`
    WHERE
        `my penalty days` MEANS IF `a penalty was imposed on me under section 35 before` THEN LIST `the day that earlier penalty was imposed` ELSE EMPTY

-- Regs s 35(3): 15% (first violation) or 50% (subsequent) of twelve times the basic amount for the payment period of the violation, worked out
-- under section 6 without any reduction for income. The index is asked for 2024 to 2026 (see the basic-amount question).
@export How large could my penalty be (Regs s 35(3))?
GIVEN `this is a first violation for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a first violation for you? (See the question about first violations.)
      `the day I committed the violation` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you commit the violation?
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2024` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada for 2024 (annual average, not seasonally adjusted, as Statistics Canada publishes it)?
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2025` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2025? (0 if it is not yet published)
      `the Consumer Price Index for 2026` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that index for 2026? (0 if it is not yet published)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How large could my penalty be` IS
    `the penalty the Minister may issue` `this is a first violation for me` `the day I committed the violation` `my figures`
    WHERE
        `my figures` MEANS filter `has been published` (LIST `the 2024 figure`, `the 2025 figure`, `the 2026 figure`)
        `has been published` f MEANS f's `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` GREATER THAN 0
        `the 2024 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2024, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2024`
        `the 2025 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2025, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2025`
        `the 2026 figure` MEANS `Consumer Price Index figure` WITH `the calendar year of the figure` IS 2026, `the annual average all-items Consumer Price Index for Canada, not seasonally adjusted` IS `the Consumer Price Index for 2026`

@export Can the Minister cancel a penalty imposed on me (Regs s 35(7))?
GIVEN `new facts are presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are new facts presented?
      `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on a mistake as to, some material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister cancel a penalty imposed on me` IF
    `the Minister may rescind the penalty` `new facts are presented` `the Minister is satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on a mistake as to, some material fact`

-- The Regulations set no fine and no term of imprisonment for these offences: see NOTES.md.
@export Am I guilty of an offence (Regs s 36(1))?
GIVEN `I knowingly used false identity information or another person's information to obtain a benefit for myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly use false identity information, or another person's information, to obtain a benefit for yourself?
      `I counselled a person to apply for a benefit with the intent to steal all or a substantial part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you counsel a person to apply for a benefit with the intent to steal all or a substantial part of it?
      `I knowingly made false or misleading representations in relation to an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly make false or misleading representations in relation to an application for a benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` `I knowingly used false identity information or another person's information to obtain a benefit for myself` `I counselled a person to apply for a benefit with the intent to steal all or a substantial part of it` `I knowingly made false or misleading representations in relation to an application`

@export Can I still be prosecuted for an act if a penalty was imposed for it (Regs s 36(2))?
GIVEN `a penalty for the act has been imposed on me under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a penalty for the act been imposed on you under section 35?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still be prosecuted for an act if a penalty was imposed for it` IF
    `a proceeding may be commenced under section 36 or the Criminal Code for the act` `a penalty for the act has been imposed on me under section 35`


§§ `Act s 9 and Regulations ss 37 to 40 -- Overpayments, debts and recovery`

@export Can my benefit be taken to pay another debt or claim (Act s 9)?
GIVEN `the claim against my benefit` IS A `Claim against a benefit` @desc What kind of claim is it: a bankruptcy or insolvency law, an assignment, charge, attachment or giving as security, a deduction or set-off under another Act of Parliament, a deduction or set-off under this Act, a garnishment under the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act, or any other claim?
GIVETH A `Position of a benefit against a claim`
DECIDE `Can my benefit be taken to pay another debt or claim` IS
    `how the benefit stands against the claim` `the claim against my benefit`

@export What do I owe if I was paid more than I was entitled to (Regs s 37(1))?
GIVEN `the benefit payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in benefit payments did you receive, in dollars?
      `the benefit I was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much benefit were you entitled to, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What do I owe if I was paid more than I was entitled to` IS
    `the amount that must be returned` `the benefit payments I received` `the benefit I was entitled to`

@export From what day is the overpayment a debt I owe (Regs s 37(2))?
GIVEN `the benefit payments I received` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in benefit payments did you receive, in dollars?
      `the benefit I was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much benefit were you entitled to, in dollars?
      `the day the payment was made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the payment made?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what day is the overpayment a debt I owe` IS
    `the day from which the erroneous payment or overpayment is a debt due to His Majesty` `the benefit payments I received` `the benefit I was entitled to` `the day the payment was made`

@export Can I pay what I owe in instalments (Regs s 37(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister agrees to instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister agree to instalments?
      `each instalment is an amount that does not cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is each instalment an amount that does not cause you undue hardship?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I pay what I owe in instalments` IF
    `the debt may be paid in instalments` `the Minister agrees to instalments` `each instalment is an amount that does not cause me undue hardship`

@export Will I be charged interest on what I owe (Regs s 37(4), 37(5))?
GIVEN `the payment was made because of a violation penalised under section 35 or an offence for which a fine or imprisonment was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made as a result of a violation for which a penalty was imposed under section 35, or an offence for which a fine or a term of imprisonment was imposed under the Criminal Code?
      `I can still ask for reconsideration or judicial review or appeal, or one is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you still make a request for reconsideration, an application for judicial review or an appeal about it, or is one pending?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be charged interest on what I owe` IF
    `interest is payable on the amount owing` `the payment was made because of a violation penalised under section 35 or an offence for which a fine or imprisonment was imposed` `I can still ask for reconsideration or judicial review or appeal, or one is pending`

@export From what day is a penalty I was given a debt I owe (Regs s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the day the penalty was imposed on me` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the penalty imposed on you?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day is a penalty I was given a debt I owe` IS
    `the day from which a penalty is a debt due to His Majesty` `the day the penalty was imposed on me`

@export Does interest run on my penalty (Regs s 38(2))?
GIVEN `I can still ask for reconsideration or judicial review or appeal about the penalty, or one is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you still make a request for reconsideration, an application for judicial review or an appeal about the penalty, or is one pending?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest run on my penalty` IF
    `interest accrues on the penalty debt` `I can still ask for reconsideration or judicial review or appeal about the penalty, or one is pending`

@export By what day must action be taken to recover money I owe (Regs s 39(1), 39(2))?
GIVEN `the day the money became due and payable` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the money become due and payable?
      `the number of days the six-year period stopped running` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days was the six-year period suspended (because an action was prohibited or a review was pending)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must action be taken to recover money I owe` IS
    `the last day on which an action to recover money may be taken` `the day the money became due and payable` `the number of days the six-year period stopped running`

@export Does the six-year limit apply to the proceedings against me (Regs s 39(3))?
GIVEN `the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the six-year limit apply to the proceedings against me` IF
    `the six-year limitation period applies` `the proceedings relate to the execution, renewal or enforcement of a judgment`

@export When may the Minister certify what I owe (Regs s 40(1))?
GIVEN `the day I defaulted` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you default?
      `the Minister is of the opinion that I am attempting to avoid payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister of the opinion that you are attempting to avoid payment?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When may the Minister certify what I owe` IS
    `the earliest day on which the unrecovered debt may be certified` `the day I defaulted` `the Minister is of the opinion that I am attempting to avoid payment`

@export Can the Minister take money that someone owes me (Regs s 40(6))?
GIVEN `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted to me or liable to pay me, and I am liable to pay His Majesty under the Act or Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Minister know or suspect that a person is or is about to become indebted to you or liable to make a payment to you, while you are liable to pay His Majesty under the Act or the Regulations?
      `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Minister take money that someone owes me` IF
    `the Minister may require the money to be paid to the Receiver General` `the Minister knows or suspects that a person is or is about to become indebted to me or liable to pay me, and I am liable to pay His Majesty under the Act or Regulations` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`

@export If someone does not pay the Minister as a garnishment notice requires, is the amount a debt (Regs s 40(7))?
GIVEN `the amount was required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)?
      `the amount was not paid as the notice required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount not paid as the notice required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount not paid as a garnishment notice requires a debt due to His Majesty` IF
    `the unpaid amount is a debt due to His Majesty` `the amount was required to be paid by a notice under subsection 40(6)` `the amount was not paid as the notice required`
